        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Benefit-risk assessment is how regulators such as the FDA and EMA judge whether a medicine&apos;s benefits outweigh its harms, given the uncertainties.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Benefit-Risk Assessment</skos:prefLabel>
