        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">GEE</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Generalized estimating equations are a regression approach for estimating population-averaged associations from correlated observations by specifying a marginal mean model and accounting for within-cluster dependence.</skos:definition>
