        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Lost to Follow-Up</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Loss to follow-up occurs when trial participants stop providing data before follow-up ends, so later outcomes, costs and QALYs can be missing.</skos:definition>
