        <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mixed effects model combines population-level fixed coefficients with probability-modelled variation across groups or individuals to analyse outcomes with clustered or repeated observations.</skos:definition>
